The Broker led the [[Org/Althane/The Network|Network]], and his name was the one its clients knew best. His true name is T3C, said aloud as "Tech"; like every warforged's, it is written in capitals and digits. He is of [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]]. Since he took up an [[Phenomena/Echo Fragment|Echo Fragment]], no one remembers him. He goes on in an echo-fragmented form, impossible to observe or touch. Sedecium has followed the trail he leaves for its whole history without knowing what it is, and calls it the entity.

A hood is drawn up over his face; beneath it he is dark metal with wooden fittings, and a symbol no one has read is stamped into his forehead. He belonged to no local [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]], so a mage felt nothing of him. He travels by a flash of blue light. He knows a magic that rewrites a witness's memory, and kept a short list of loose ends he meant to close.

He kept to himself, working through the handlers of his cells. A library served as his own, book stacks on either side of a long table; a two-headed dragon, [[People/Althane/Terexanthes|Terexanthes]], stands with him there, and so does a man in a suit whose head is a burst of green flame. When scrying spells fell twice on one of the Broker's people, the Broker pulled that operative back. He took the artifacts that saw [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] framed and blamed for the theft, and handed them to [[People/Althane/Rowan|Rowan]] to put away. His rooms in [[Geography/Althane/Illyara/index|Illyara]] belong to [[People/Althane/Oxas|Oxas]]. He cuts chrome into his own people. He kept a surgery theater in [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Terminus|Terminus]], where he worked alone, strapping a client down and guiding the tools with a gloved hand, opening the skull, fitting the implant, and knitting the bone back with a little necromancy. The same hand did the work on his own head, and he trusted no one else with it.

Sedecium's people come from the antimatter world of [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]] and wear charms to keep from destroying ordinary matter at a touch. T3C was one of the party on Ushas that killed [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]], with [[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]], [[People/Zugg|Zugg]] and [[People/Rotok|Rotok]]. Afterwards he worked out a way to walk from one crystal sphere to the next, and walked away from Ushas to gather information for Sedecium, whose goal is to destroy the Thessians. He kept a citadel in open space, [[Geography/Elysium|Elysium]], and carried a dead [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]], one of the good ones, tethered to him.

He hunted an Echo Fragment against the will of [[Divinity/The Narrative/index|the Narrative]]. He had gone to take one from the thing at the centre of Althane, and [[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] had shot him with a weapon that left a wound he could not heal. It would not kill him, but until Karkov was dead or the weapon destroyed he could neither fight the Stranger nor teleport away. Through Oxas the Broker hired [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] in Illyara, and after one more mission brought them into his great task. He also hired them to recover the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] out of the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]]. The Weft agreed to help, and found their way into Oresk through the Leviathan, where they fought at the Night Market, lost [[People/Althane/Big Fish|Big Fish]], found [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawn]] in an alternate wick, and stole the Kaathe [[People/Althane/YuDaan|YuDaan]].

When the Weft defeated [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Feep]] they gave its Echo Fragment to T3C. He took it up, and it gave him the one thing he had wanted all along: it made him a god, and it tore him out of every record, so that he vanished from the Weft's memories too. That is why the records of him are stripped. The pavilion of statues at Sedecium counts three where it once counted four. He fought a [[Bestiary/False Hydra|false hydra]] and took from it the power to be forgotten. The trail he leaves has led Sedecium to weapons, lost systems and new allies, and it led a Sedecium crew to [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/index|Inevitable Everdawn]], an old Sundom station adrift in [[Phenomena/The Slip|the slip]].
